            "bit_cutoff" : 85,
            "comment" : "N-terminal furin product of the glycoprotein precursor: Richt 1998 (PMID 9557754) places the cut after Arg249 of the 503 aa BoDV-1 protein. Its bit cutoff is 85 by MEASUREMENT, not by default. On the one Cartilovirus genome the G_N profiles also fire inside Vp1, an ancient duplication of the glycoprotein that carries its own furin site (PMID 38028148), giving a second G_N call; that false call peaks at 69 bits while true G_N calls score 103-527 across all four genera, so 85 sits in the gap. The non_pssm_partner construction was tried first and is worse: call_non_pssm_features pairs every G and G_C HSP, which put 6-16 spurious G_N calls on every exemplar. It retains the signal peptide -- no mature N-terminus has been determined for any bornavirus glycoprotein.",
